      "title": "File:The Tomb of the Eagles - geograph.org.uk - 1452411.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/The_Tomb_of_the_Eagles_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1452411.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Tomb_of_the_Eagles_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1452411.jpg",
      "width": 640,
      "height": 428,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Stephen McKay",
      "description": "The Tomb of the Eagles This neolithic burial chamber was found by a farmer when the stones were uncovered following a storm. His family still owns the land and access is via a visitor centre at South Liddel. The 5,000 year old cairn gets its name from the talons of sea eagles that were found with the human remains - they may have been hunting trophies but if so it is not known what methods were used to hunt such fearsome creatures. It is possible to enter the chamber using a narrow entrance close to where the visitors are standing.",
      "dateCreated": "2009-08-12",
